oopener noreferrer\">Health Investment News</a></li><li><a href=\"/news/industry/health-startups\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Health Startup News</a></li><li><a href=\"/news/industry/medical-devices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Medical Devices News</a></li><li><a href=\"/news/industry/pharma\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pharma News</a><ul><li><a href=\"/news/industry/pharma/cdsco\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CDSCO (Central Drugs Standard Control Organisation) News</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"/news/industry/pharmacy-education\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pharmacy Education  News</a></li><li><a href=\"/news/industry/aiandhealth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AI and healthcare</a></li><li><a href=\"/news/industry/industry-perspective\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Industry Perspective</a></li></ul></li><li></li></ul><figure><!-- !{Utils.getMediaElement(data,0)}--><img src=\"https://medicaldialogues.in/h-upload/2024/01/16/230297-sun-pharma-new-50.webp\" alt=\"Sun Pharma Q2 Profit Falls 36%, Revenue Rises to Rs 16,199 Crore\" title=\"Sun Pharma Q2 Profit Falls 36%, Revenue Rises to Rs 16,199 Crore\"></figure><p>New Delhi: The National Pharmaceutical Pricing Authority (NPPA) has specified a retail price of Rs. 6.25 per gram for Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Limited's Diclofenac, Methyl Salicylate and Menthol Gel.</p><p>The development follows a corrigendum issued by the authority under the Department of Pharmaceuticals, Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, through S.O. 6002(E), dated November 2, 2026.</p><p>The corrigendum revises the entry at serial number 35 in the retail price notification published in the Gazette of India, Extraordinary, vide S.O. 5638(E), dated November 2, 2018.</p><p>The formulation contains Diclofenac Diethylamine BP 2.32% w/w, equivalent to Diclofenac Sodium 2% w/w, along with Methyl Salicylate IP 10% w/w and Menthol IP 5% w/w. The notification lists Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd. as the manufacturer and marketing company.</p><p>Diclofenac, methyl salicylate, and menthol gel is a combination topical medication used to relieve localized muscle and joint pain, inflammation, and stiffness.</p><p>Sl. No.</p><p>Name of the Formulation / Brand Name</p><p>Strength</p><p>Unit</p><p>Manufacturer &amp; Marketing Company</p><p>Retail Price (₹)</p><p>(1)</p><p>(2)</p><p>(3)</p><p>(4)</p><p>(5)</p><p>(6)</p><p>35</p><p>Diclofenac + Methyl + Menthol GEL</p><p>Contains: Diclofenac Diethylamine BP 2.32% w/w (eq. to Diclofenac Sodium 2% w/w), Methyl Salcylate IP 10% w/w &amp; Menthol IP 5% w/w</p><p>1 Gram</p><p>M/s Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd.</p><p>6.25</p><p>Furthermore, the notice added,</p><p>\"2. Further, the entries against serial numbers 36, 51 and 52 in the Table of the said notification shall stand deleted.</p><p>3. All the notes and other contents mentioned in the original order S.O. 5638(E), dated 02.11.2018 relating to Sl. No.35 of the table shall remain the same.\"</p><p>To view the notice, click the link below:</p><p><a href=\"/author/susmita-roy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"/images/authorplaceholder.jpg\" alt=\"Susmita Roy\" title=\"Susmita Roy\"></a></p><h3>Mpharm (Pharmacology)        </h3><p>Susmita Roy, B pharm, M pharm Pharmacology, graduated from Gurunanak Institute of Pharmaceutical Science and Technology with a bachelor's degree in Pharmacy. She is currently working as an assistant professor at Haldia Institute of Pharmacy in West Bengal. She has been part of Medical Dialogues since March 2021.</p><p><img src=\"/images/logo.svg\"></p><p>Next Story</p><p>NO DATA FOUND</p>"
